v0.11.0: schema trust contract — boot-time drift detection

Six consecutive hotfixes (v0.10.15 → v0.10.29) on variations of
the same underlying bug: the code assumed X but the DB shipped Y.
Every one would have been caught at deploy line by a substrate
that walks the code's schema assumptions against the actual DB
state at boot.

  v0.10.15  agents.owner_id (never existed)
  v0.10.16  fork.rs owner_id (same)
  v0.10.18  agents.updated_at (mig-166 shipped)
  v0.10.19  resolve_forecast() returns REAL not FLOAT8
  v0.10.27  mig-166 never actually applied — PgBouncer ate DO $$
  v0.10.29  JSON case: "Error" vs "error" (wire drift, not schema)

Five of six are schema drift. This release ships the substrate.

Change:

  src/schema_trust.rs (new)
    * SCHEMA_TABLES:    ~40 tables the code SELECTs / INSERTs / FKs against
    * SCHEMA_COLUMNS:   ~70 columns whose absence produces user-facing 500s
                        (expanded 14× from the existing 5-entry list)
    * SCHEMA_FUNCTIONS: 4 functions with args AND return-type checks
                        (return-type field is new — catches v0.10.19)
    * verify(db) -> SchemaVerdict with itemized drift lists
    * emit_boot_report(v, strict) -> BootDecision (Healthy /
                                     DriftContinueBoot / DriftAbortBoot)
    * verify_and_report(db) — one-call convenience

  src/api_server.rs::main
    * boot-time invocation after run_migrations + ensure_critical_schema
    * SCHEMA_STRICT=1 → exit(2) on drift (production-strict posture)
    * SCHEMA_STRICT unset → log-loud-and-continue (rollout mode)
    * mod schema_trust registered

  src/handlers/admin.rs
    * admin_schema_health_handler refactored to delegate to
      schema_trust::verify (5 lines). Response body shape preserved
      (backwards compatible with existing dashboard).
    * legacy inline body cfg'd out (#[cfg(any())]) — can be deleted
      after operators confirm the new handler output is a superset.

Modes:

  Default (SCHEMA_STRICT unset)
    Warn-loud-and-continue. On drift, stderr shows a boxed banner
    plus one line per issue. Deploy still serves traffic — the
    operator sees the drift in Railway logs immediately instead
    of on the first user click.

  Strict (SCHEMA_STRICT=1)
    Same banner + itemized list, then exit(2). Railway restarts
    the container; if the drift persists, boot loops. Intended
    posture once the contract is production-quiet.

Rule for adding entries to SCHEMA_COLUMNS:
  If losing this column would produce a user-facing 500, it
  belongs here.

Would-have-caught coverage:
  5 of 6 v0.10.x schema-drift bugs → yes (schema axis)
  1 of 6 (v0.10.29 case drift)     → no (wire-format axis — v0.12.0)

Not in scope:
  * Wire-format (Rust↔JS case) drift check — v0.12.0 candidate.
  * Auto-populate SCHEMA_COLUMNS from build.rs. Hand-declared
    is high signal / low false-positive to start.
  * Query-plan drift check. Useful once tables get big.

Related:
  scripts/lint-schema-consistency.py  — sibling: catches drift at
                                        commit time (pre-deploy)
  ensure_critical_schema              — sibling: lands columns at
                                        boot via single-statement ALTERs

Three substrates now, one substrate mission: DB and code agree
on what exists.
